ut gotcha (Astronomy Engine rotation transpose)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ASTRONOMY.md", "source_location": "L52", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "RotateVector uses rot[j][i], so aeRotToM3 transposes into row-major; a test checks it to 1e-15."}, {"id": "docs_astronomy_earth_matrix", "label": "earthMatrix = S\u00b7(PN\u00b7Rz(GAST))\u00b7S\u1d40", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ASTRONOMY.md", "source_location": "L57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "three's SphereGeometry UVs already equal S\u00b7EF, so the equirectangular texture needs no offset."}, {"id": "docs_astronomy_static_sky", "label": "Static sky, moving Earth", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ASTRONOMY.md", "source_location": "L75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stars and grids are placed once in J2000 scene coordinates; precession and nutation show up as the Earth's axis moving inside the fixed sky."}, {"id": "docs_astronomy_observer_geodetic_pin", "label": "Geodetic observer pin on a unit sphere with ENU basis", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ASTRONOMY.md", "source_location": "L82", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pin normal equals the WGS84 geodetic zenith so altitudes match Astronomy Engine; costs at most ~21 km of position error."}, {"id": "docs_astronomy_light_time_correction", "label": "Light-time correction", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ASTRONOMY.md", "source_location": "L120", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_astronomy_topocentric_parallax", "label": "Topocentric directions (Moon parallax ~1\u00b0)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ASTRONOMY.md", "source_location": "L123", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_astronomy_astrometric_vs_apparent", "label": "Astrometric J2000 drawing vs apparent of-date tables", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ASTRONOMY.md", "source_location": "L146", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The star catalogue is astrometric J2000, so beams drawn in that frame land on the right stars; tables show what an observer measures. Difference: aberration <= 20.5 arcsec plus refraction."}, {"id": "docs_astronomy_true_scale_moon", "label": "True-scale Moon (IAU rotation, libration, Lommel\u2013Seeliger lighting)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ASTRONOMY.md", "source_location": "L156", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Phase and libration are correct by construction from geometry, not drawn from MoonPhase."}, {"id": "docs_astronomy_star_colour_model", "label": "Star colour from B\u2212V (Ballesteros + Planck \u00d7 CIE 1931)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ASTRONOMY.md", "source_location": "L177", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_astronomy_refraction_model", "label": "S\u00e6mundsson refraction (refractionDeg)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ASTRONOMY.md", "source_location": "L191", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mirrors Astronomy Engine's Refraction('normal', h) exactly so the frame pass and AE.Horizon tables agree."}, {"id": "docs_astronomy_airmass_extinction", "label": "Airmass and extinction (Kasten\u2013Young, k = 0.2 mag)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ASTRONOMY.md", "source_location": "L195", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_astronomy_twilight_classes", "label": "Twilight classes by solar altitude", "file_type": "concept", "source_